<main>
<header class="b063-header"><a class="b063-brand" href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab">Sports Edge Lab</a><span>NCAA men &amp; women · Preserved science · B063 recovery edition</span></header>
<p class="b063-eyebrow">Evidence first · November 11, 2026</p>
<h1>Keep the work.<br><span>Make the evidence visible.</span></h1>
<p class="b063-intro">Compare the saved historical leaders, inspect every retained source game, and revisit original issued forecasts without changing their timestamps. The legacy models and their stronger results remain available.</p>
<nav class="b063-pills" aria-label="NCAA report sections"><a href="#b063-scorecards">Season scorecards</a><a href="#b063-role-section">Champion roles</a><a href="#b063-market-section">Market comparisons</a><a href="#b063-game-section">All saved games</a><a href="#b063-archive-section">Original issue archive</a><a href="#b063-legacy">Dated previous review</a></nav>
<section class="b063-summary" aria-label="Preserved evidence counts"><div class="b063-stat"><b>3,457</b><span>saved source records · not a certified unique-game denominator</span></div><div class="b063-stat"><b>814</b><span>completed-game frozen replay triplets · retrospective evidence</span></div><div class="b063-stat"><b>32</b><span>original issued game identities · 30 matched to later outcomes</span></div></section>
<section class="b063-notice" aria-label="B063 execution status"><h2>B063 engineering recovery is in progress</h2><p><strong>No new owner fit, forecast issue, model promotion or measured 12-worker speedup is claimed by this publication.</strong> Live B062 state and a completed B063 owner return still need authenticated reconciliation. The dashboard below uses preserved B060/B061 science exposed in the B062 handoff reports.</p><p>Scientific evidence cutoff: <strong id="b063-evidence-time"></strong><br>Observed-game census cutoff: <span id="b063-census-time"></span>. Republishing a saved record does not refresh its source data or change its original issue time.</p></section>
<div class="b063-controls" aria-label="League and season filters"><label>League<select id="b063-league"><option value="all">Men and women</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></label><label>Season<select id="b063-season"><option value="all">All saved seasons</option><option value="2025">2024–25 historical</option><option value="2026">2025–26 historical</option><option value="2027">2026–27 current</option></select></label></div>
<section id="b063-scorecards" class="b063-section"><h2>Season scorecards</h2><h3>Completed seasons · saved metric leaders</h3><p class="b063-note">Each column may identify a different model. These are exposed historical research results, not a single champion's seven-metric scorecard. Equal row counts do not prove paired membership. Full precision is preserved in the source export.</p><div id="b063-historical"></div><h3>2026–27 · original frozen replay and preserved issued forecasts</h3><p class="b063-note">Reconstruction and original issuance are separate evidence modes and are never pooled here. The 415 men's and 399 women's replay games reproduce the remembered 0.394807 and 0.318015 log loss. The issued cohorts are much smaller. Independent official-final qualification remains incomplete.</p><div id="b063-current"></div><div class="b063-two"><article><h3>Why a .40 and a .66 can coexist</h3><p>The same frozen men's reference has log loss 0.661434 on 175 games with pick confidence below 80%, versus 0.394807 on all 415 games. The women's values are 0.623177 on 159 lower-confidence games and 0.318015 on all 399. Both full samples include 240 higher-confidence games. Cohort difficulty changes the headline without changing the model.</p></article><article><h3>What has not been established</h3><p>This saved evidence does not prove a newly refreshed champion across the entire current season, every official game, all three market providers, or genuinely issued rolling forecasts for every game. A historical score alone is insufficient for promotion.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="b063-role-section" class="b063-section"><h2>Champion roles and promotion evidence</h2><p class="b063-note">Six preserved historical selections are authenticated in this saved ledger: probability log loss, margin MAE and total MAE for each league. The planned fourteen-role comparison additionally separates accuracy, Brier, margin RMSE and total RMSE. Missing role selections remain missing. These aliases retain the original selection basis and confer no new promotion.</p><div id="b063-roles"></div><h3>Rolling champions</h3><p class="b063-note">A newly qualified per-game rolling-champion table is not supplied by these saved sources. Original forecasts, frozen-model replay, exposed rolling reconstruction and genuine future issues must keep their own training, source and issue clocks. Previously recorded rolling work remains in the dated review below; its counts do not fill absent game-level rows.</p><details><summary>What must be true before promotion?</summary><ol><li>Authenticate the model, features, training membership and information clocks.</li><li>Compare candidate and incumbent on identical eligible games, target, horizon and settlement rules.</li><li>Follow the frozen 2024–25 and 2025–26 selection policy; disclose historical research exposure.</li><li>Keep 2026–27 monitoring and genuinely future issues separate from historical reconstruction.</li><li>Require meaningful, stable improvement with uncertainty and operational reproducibility. No automatic promotion follows from the scores above.</li></ol></details></section>
<section id="b063-market-section" class="b063-section"><h2>DraftKings, Kalshi and Polymarket</h2><p class="b063-note">A provider-specific matched cohort is required for every comparison. Missing markets are not zeros, and one provider's sample cannot stand in for another's. The preserved Polymarket International sample has slightly higher model winner accuracy but lower market log loss. The market's half-credit tie convention remains intact.</p><div id="b063-markets"></div><p class="b063-note">No complete three-provider leaderboard across 2024–25, 2025–26 and the entire current season is established here. Polymarket International and Polymarket US remain distinct. Per-game paired market values are unavailable in this saved census.</p></section>
<section id="b063-game-section" class="b063-section"><h2>All saved source games</h2><p class="b063-note">Every one of the 3,457 retained source records is available below. These include unresolved source identities and unmatched official candidates. The census is not a complete certified season. “Upcoming” means future at the saved source cutoff; this page does not fetch live schedules. Home margin is home points minus away points. Blank predictions are unavailable, including all unissued future previews.</p><div class="b063-controls"><label>Record population<select id="b063-status"><option value="all">All source records</option><option value="completed">Observed completed records</option><option value="future">Upcoming at source cutoff</option><option value="issued">Exactly bound original issues</option><option value="replay">Completed frozen replay</option><option value="unresolved">Unmatched / unresolved identity</option></select></label><label>Prediction evidence<select id="b063-mode"><option value="issued">Preserved original issues</option><option value="replay">Frozen original replay</option></select></label><label class="b063-search">Find team or event<input id="b063-query" type="search" placeholder="Team name or source event ID"></label><button id="b063-reset" type="button">Show all records</button><button id="b063-download" type="button">Download filtered CSV</button></div><div class="b063-paging"><p id="b063-game-count" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="b063-prev" type="button">Previous</button><button id="b063-next" type="button">Next</button></div><div id="b063-game-table"></div><div id="b063-detail" class="b063-detail" hidden></div></section>
<section id="b063-archive-section" class="b063-section"><h2>Preserved original issue archive</h2><p class="b063-note">All 96 selected target outputs retain their original model-role alias, prediction and issue clocks. Two game identities have changed recorded tip times without authenticated alias history: their six forecasts remain here, without borrowing later outcomes or being silently dropped. Current-champion status remains unqualified.</p><div class="b063-controls"><label>Target<select id="b063-archive-target"><option value="win">Winner probability</option><option value="margin">Margin</option><option value="total">Total points</option><option value="all">All 96 target records</option></select></label><p id="b063-archive-count" class="b063-note" aria-live="polite"></p></div><div id="b063-archive"></div></section>
<details id="b063-legacy" class="b063-legacy"><summary>Preserved previous dashboard · dated B058 and earlier evidence</summary><p class="b063-note">The following page is retained as a dated archive. Its “latest” labels refer to that earlier publication, not this recovery edition. Original populations, findings, methods and private-report tooling remain intact.</p><div class="b063-legacy-content">__B063_LEGACY__</div></details>
<footer class="b063-footer">Built by Alvaro Mendizabal · NCAA men and women only.<br>Source snapshot: <a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/268d9db3752a93ed089821350c664ce3b9293653/examples/ncaa_review">pinned preserved evidence</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/B063_DASHBOARD_STATUS.md">publication status</a> · <a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/docs/PUBLICATION_BOUNDARY.md">reporting scope</a><br>Static, self-contained report. No live provider calls, external scripts, raw feeds or model weights. GitHub source publication and website deployment are separate events.</footer>
